& \Rightarrow \frac{x d v}{d x}=\frac{3 v^2}{1-2 v} \Rightarrow\left(\frac{1}{3 v^2}-\frac{2}{3 v}\right) d v=\frac{d x}{x}
\end{aligned}$<br/>Integrating we get, $\frac{-1}{3 v}-\frac{2}{3} \log v=\log x+\log c_1$
$\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \frac{-x}{y}-2 \log \frac{y}{x}=3 \log x+\log c_2 \\
& \Rightarrow \frac{-x}{y}=\log c_2 x+2 \log y \Rightarrow \frac{-x}{y}=\log c_2 x y^2 \\
& \Rightarrow e^{-\frac{x}{y}}=c x y^2 \Rightarrow c x y^2 e^{\frac{x}{y}}=1
\end{aligned}$

